= The Dublin Summit

At the European Council in Dublin, the other heads of government offer to refund a third of Britain's excess contribution to the Community budget. Britain pays in far more than any other member except West Germany, despite being one of the poorer ones.

- @money_back: "I want my money back."
- @accept: Take the offer and keep the peace.

@money_back
on-arrival: eec_rebate += 1; europe_relation -= 12; thatcher_rating += 3; c2_con += 2*(1-dissent); right_dissent -= 3; wet_dissent += 2

You refuse the offer and lecture the summit for hours. Chancellor Schmidt pretends to fall asleep. The British papers love it.

@accept
on-arrival: europe_relation += 6; budget += 0.5; right_dissent += 4

We accept the partial refund. Europe is relieved; our Eurosceptics are not.
